<title>GERMANY: TABLE-HWWA institute German economic forecast.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HWWA institute German economic forecast.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table contains key details of the HWWA economic research institute's economic forecast for Germany published on Tuesday.</p>
<p>(Changes in percent unless stated)</p>
<p>					   1996     1997     1998</p>
<p>PAN-GERMANY</p>
<p>    GDP (in 1991 prices)	    1.4	2.25    2.75</p>
<p>    Private consumption	     1.3	1.0     2.0</p>
<p>    State consumptiion		2.4	1.5     1.0</p>
<p>    Capitl investment		 2.4	4.5     6.5</p>
<p>    Construction investment	-2.7     -0.5     0.5</p>
<p>    Domestic demand		   0.8	1.5     2.5</p>
<p>    Exports			     4.9	8.0     6.5</p>
<p>    Imports			     2.6	5.0     5.5</p>
<p>    Workforce			  -1.2     -1.0     0.5</p>
<p>    Unemployed (million people)	 3.965    4.325   4.225</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate (percent)  10.3     11.2    11.0</p>
<p>    Retail prices		     1.5	1.5     1.5</p>
<p>    Budget deficit (pct of GDP)   3.8	3.2     2.5</p>
<p>    Current account (bln marks) -20.9    -10.0     0.0</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>WEST GERMANY</p>
<p>    GDP (in 1991 prices)	    1.3	2.25    2.75</p>
<p>    Workforce			  -1.0     -1.0     0.5</p>
<p>    Unemployed			  2.796    3.025   2.925</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate (percent)   9.0	9.7     9.4</p>
<p>    Retail prices		     1.4	1.5     1.5</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>EAST GERMANY</p>
<p>    GDP (in 1991 prices)	    2.0	2.5     3.0</p>
<p>    Workforce			  -1.7     -2.5     0.0</p>
<p>    Unemployed			  1.169    1.300   1.300</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate (percent)  15.7     17.6    17.6</p>
<p>    Retail prices		     2.2	1.75    1.25</p>
